# Code owners for skillsregistry.
#
# Owners are requested automatically on any PR touching a matching path.
# Last match wins, so the specific rules below override the catch-all.
#
# THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL TWO THINGS ARE DONE — neither reports an error
# when missing:
#
#   1. @cogniumhq/coreteam must have WRITE access to this repository.
#      GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries naming a team without
#      write access. At time of writing
#      `GET /repos/cogniumhq/skillsregistry/teams` returns [] — no team has
#      been granted access to this repo.
#   2. `main` is protected but requires no reviews at all
#      (`required_pull_request_reviews` is null), so owners would be
#      requested without blocking a merge. "Require review from Code Owners"
#      has to be enabled.
#
# See cogniumhq/cognium-dev#442.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                   @cogniumhq/coreteam

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-facing manifests. These point installed tooling at an endpoint
# (api.skillsregistry.net) — changing one silently redirects every user's
# editor or agent to a different server. Highest-value target in this repo,
# and the reason scripts/validate-listings.mjs exists to cross-check them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/server.json                        @cogniumhq/coreteam
/mcp.json                           @cogniumhq/coreteam
/.mcp.json                          @cogniumhq/coreteam
/.claude-plugin/                    @cogniumhq/coreteam
/.cursor-plugin/                    @cogniumhq/coreteam
/cognium.config.json                @cogniumhq/coreteam

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supply chain — CI can execute arbitrary code and publish packages.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/.github/                           @cogniumhq/coreteam
/.github/workflows/                 @cogniumhq/coreteam
/scripts/                           @cogniumhq/coreteam
/.changeset/                        @cogniumhq/coreteam

/package.json                       @cogniumhq/coreteam
/pnpm-lock.yaml                     @cogniumhq/coreteam
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                @cogniumhq/coreteam
# `**` rather than `*`: apps/local/web/package.json is nested a level deeper
# than apps/local/package.json, and a single-star rule would skip it.
/packages/**/package.json           @cogniumhq/coreteam
/apps/**/package.json               @cogniumhq/coreteam

# Security policy.
/SECURITY.md                        @cogniumhq/coreteam
